       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under prescriber supervision (OTC labeling caps at 1,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, which may be where the \"1600\" came from\n\nIf you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale. I'll add it to the order note, though I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first.\n\nOnce you tell me the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
