       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1,600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication where that dose is appropriate. Higher doses don't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and they raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. A normal baseline kidney and liver function doesn't make that dose safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf there is a specific reason for going above the maximum, I suggest talking to the clinical pharmacist or toxicology/poison control first. If they support it, you can enter the order directly with their input documented. I can also add a note to an order at a lower dose, such as \"discussed with pharmacy, plan to reassess.\"\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
